  "description": "<p>The Fedora ontology is available online, but LDP clients have a hard time parsing it since it doesn't include a Content-Type header. It really MUST return a Content-Type header. I see that most other ontologies will redirect clients to a URL with a .rdf extension.</p>\n\n<p>For example:</p>\n\n<p>$ curl -i <a href=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/2016/03/01/repository\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/2016/03/01/repository</a></p>\n\n<p>HTTP/1.1 200 OK<br/>\nDate: Sun, 31 Jul 2016 13:09:56 GMT<br/>\nServer: Apache<br/>\nLast-Modified: Mon, 02 May 2016 15:50:16 GMT<br/>\nETag: \"621a-531ddf2e5c191\"<br/>\nAccept-Ranges: bytes<br/>\nContent-Length: 25114</p>",
